  "mujoco_changes": "2026-10-12, on the soft contact class at a constant impedance: the one-hand hang instead of the fold (stages hang_release_table_pickup_stages, prefix hang {lift_m 0.32, pull_over}). The released route could not start on MuJoCo: at the birth the ring's wire lies inside the open left jaw at the left shoe's outer bend, so the left shoe cannot be grasped there, and the recorded fold fails from every other grasp (docs/rcb/families/horseshoe_ring.md). Now the right hand alone lifts the right shoe 0.32 m (its recorded grasp); the chain links and the left shoe hang from it, and the ring, which lies around the left shoe's eye end and both links, hangs on the hanging shoe. The left hand grasps the ring (a grasp from which the descent over the hanging shoe is reachable), brings it level around the links above the shoe (joint search; the shoe is an obstacle, the links pass through the ring), lowers it along the hanging axis past the shoe's bend (the bore's long axis along the shoe's width) and carries it into the goal. The right hand never lets go. The task, its separator and its success rule are unchanged."
